{"schemaVersion":2,"info":"Fantastika program","schedule":[{"id":"477","title":"From conspiracy to inspiration","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"16:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0755","name":"Patrik  Centerwall (moderator)"},{"id":"0731","name":"Gunilla Jonsson"},{"id":"0748","name":"P\u00e5l  Eggert"}],"desc":"<p>That the space missions are fake became a good movie in Capricorn One 1977 (documentary!?). This year in the movie Disclosure Day the world finds out that there are aliens among us. The world is full of conspiracy theories. Which ones would work well as a starting point for a sci-fi story?<\/p>\r\n<p>This panel will only be carried out if the ruling lizards allow it!!<\/p>\r\n<p>-<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"479","title":"Food in SFF","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Interview\/Dialogue","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"17:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0746","name":"Stefan H\u00f6gberg"},{"id":"0756","name":"Regina Kanyu Wang"}],"desc":"<p><span style=\"color: #080809; font-family: 'Segoe UI Historic', 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #f0f2f5;\"><span style=\"color: #080809; font-family: Segoe UI Historic, Segoe UI, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\">You have to eat, otherwise you die,&rdquo; is a Swedish saying. How are food, conventions around eating, restaurants, etc., depicted in sci-fi and fantasy? Soylent Green or zombies eating brains, tiny pills, strange alien ingredients and dishes, abundance or scarcity and rationing?<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"480","title":"SF 100 years - Amazing Stories started 1926","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"17:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0717","name":"John-Henri Holmberg"}],"desc":"<p>The birth of science fiction has been set to ancient Greece, publication of Frankenstein etcetera, but it cannot be denied that as a popular literary form it started with the publication of the first American sf magazine, Amazing Stories. The letter columns describe the views of readers and were also used for connecting fans, leading to fandom. What did the magazine mean for the early readers and writers of sf? Did the magazine and its followers help to form a literary genre, and was this good or bad for the quality?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"481","title":"Bokcirklar - vad \u00e4r de bra f\u00f6r?","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Discussion Group","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"10:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"tomas","name":"Tomas Cronholm"}],"desc":"<p>Bokcirklar om sf och fantasy finns p&aring; flera st&auml;llen och i olika former. En del organiseras av en f&ouml;rening som SFSF och LSFF, andra &auml;r mer l&ouml;st organiserade inom fandom och en del har ingen anknytning alls till fans. Vi diskuterar vad som &auml;r l&auml;mplig lokal, hur ofta m&ouml;tena b&ouml;r h&aring;llas, hur de annonseras och hur boken v&auml;ljs ut. Vad fungerar och vad har blivit mindre lyckat? Och vilka &auml;r f&ouml;r- eller nackdelarna med att l&auml;sa inf&ouml;r en bokcirkel?<\/p>\r\n<p>&Auml;r ni flera som vilka ha i en bokcirkel i &Ouml;rebro, Solna eller digitalt kan du h&auml;r komma i kontakt med likasinnade.&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"482","title":"A sense of horror (GoH discussion)","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"21:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0730","name":"Michael  Petersen (moderator)"},{"id":"0734","name":"Maura McHugh"},{"id":"0735","name":"Gareth L. Powell"}],"desc":"<p>How can a sense of horror be effectively evoked in text, graphic novels or in a translated text? Our Guests of Honour discuss challenges in evoking feelings and what they are actually trying to achieve in their work.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"483","title":"Convention school: Crisis management","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Workshop","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"12:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"carolina","name":"Carolina Gomez Lagerl\u00f6f"}],"desc":"<p>Even in the case of good planning and a written Code of Conduct there can occur accidents or unfortunate situations. Examples are presented as well as possible solutions. How can a concom best prepare for the unexepected?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"484","title":"Kusliga historier","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Reading","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"20:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0720","name":"Martin Rundkvist"}],"desc":"<p>Martin Rundkvist l&auml;ser h&ouml;gt ur novellsamlingen \"En natt i lusthuset och andra kusliga noveller\" av Edith Nesbit<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"485","title":"H\u00f6gl\u00e4sning \/ Public reading","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Reading","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"20:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"tomas","name":"Tomas Cronholm (moderator)"}],"desc":"<p>F&ouml;rfattare l&auml;ser ur sina verk i h&ouml;gst 5 min var. Authors read from their works for 5 min each.<\/p>\r\n<p>If you wish to read, please write to info@fantastika2026.com.<\/p>\r\n<p>Registered: Sara Engstr&ouml;m, Gabriel Larsson, Cato Pellegrini, S Helter, Karen Lykkebo, C. John Arthur.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"488","title":"How and why to be a Worldcon volunteer","tags":["Track:ConComm","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"15:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0751","name":"Melissa  Lanning"},{"id":"brittlouise","name":"Britt-Louise Viklund"},{"id":"carolina","name":"Carolina Gomez Lagerl\u00f6f"}],"desc":"<p>Why would you want to do a lot of unpaid work? Hundreds of people put in hundreds of hours to organize worldcons. What do they get out of all their labour? How can you get involved at a level that suites you? Between 2029 and 2034 there are (as of now) three European bids: Dublin for 2029, Nantes for 2032 and Glasgow for 2034. A good opportunity for anyone interested in getting involved.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"497","title":"Vad g\u00f6r h\u00e4nderna?\/Busying the hands","tags":["Track:Maker","Division:Programming","Type:Discussion Group","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"14:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"ann","name":"Ann Olsson Rousset"}],"desc":"<p>Vi visar varandra vad vi pysslar med medan vi l&auml;ser, lyssnar, ser p&aring; tv...<\/p>\r\n<p>We show each other what we tinker with while we read, listen, watch TV...<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"501","title":"The liminal in Irish storytelling","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"17:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0713","name":"Johan Anglemark (moderator)"},{"id":"0718","name":"Gwen Frazer"},{"id":"0730","name":"Michael  Petersen"},{"id":"0734","name":"Maura McHugh"}],"desc":"<p>This conversation will explore the stories which lie on the boundary between our world and the worlds beyond within Irish storytelling. From horror to myth to folklore, Irish tales have often dealt with the uneasy uncertainty between the known and the unknown, the found and the faerie, the banal and the banshee. How does the tension between these elements strengthen stories?&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, 'Open Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;\">What parts of them are specifically Irish? <\/span><span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, 'Open Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;\">How do long-latent liminalities co-exist with modernity in contemporary Ireland? What role was storytelling in particular play in Ireland today?<\/span><\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"502","title":"Art and text in collaboration","tags":["Track:Comics","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"14:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"ann","name":"Ann Olsson Rousset (moderator)"},{"id":"0734","name":"Maura McHugh"},{"id":"0767","name":"Karl Johnsson"},{"id":"0769","name":"Maria Fr\u00f6hlich"}],"desc":"<p>How are graphic novels and illustrated books really created? The roles of the manuscript writer, the black and white artist and the colorist are presented and discussed. How and when do you start the collaboration? And how do you resolve any disagreements?<\/p>\r\n<p>The participants share experiences and may give some advice on the collaborations that have worked, or not worked for them.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"510","title":"Hur hittar man sin rollspelsgrupp?","tags":["Track:Gaming","Division:Programming","Type:Discussion Group","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"18:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"201","name":"Saga Bolund"}],"desc":"<p>Att spela rollspel &auml;r en livsstil. N&aring;gra har spelat rollspel med samma g&auml;ng under l&aring;ng tid. Men om rollspelsg&auml;nget av n&aring;gon anledning f&ouml;rsvinner, hur hittar man ett nytt? Hur g&ouml;r man om man vill starta ett nytt rollspelsg&auml;ng? Och om jag vill b&ouml;rja att spela rollspel, hur g&ouml;r jag det?<\/p>\r\n<p>Playing role-playing games is a lifestyle. Some people have played RPGs with the same group for a long time. But if the RPG group for some reason disappears, how do you find a new one? How do you go about starting a new RPG group? And if I want to start playing RPGs, how can I do that?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"513","title":"Romantasy - the fantasy of now","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"14:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0740","name":"Sari  Polvinen (moderator)"},{"id":"0727","name":"Marianna \"Kisu\"  Leikomaa"},{"id":"0765","name":"Elisabeth  Blixt"},{"id":"marika","name":"Marika"}],"desc":"<p>What is romantasy and why is it the most popular fantasy genre right now? Are there really any differences between a romantasy novel and a fantasy novel with romantic elements? Which are the best books and the most interesting authors? To what degree does this subgenre reflect the wider world or offer a sanctuary from it currently?<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"515","title":"Sf - varning eller f\u00f6rebild","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"13:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0726","name":"Eva Holmquist (moderator)"},{"id":"0738","name":"Jenny  Bristle"},{"id":"0771","name":"Mats Linder"},{"id":"0777","name":"Johan  J\u00f6nsson"}],"desc":"<p>Att skriva science fiction kan vara ett s&auml;tt att f&ouml;ra fram samh&auml;llskritik, visa p&aring; faror eller presentera exempel p&aring; goda samh&auml;llsbyggen. Det finns massor av exempel, d&auml;r t ex k&ouml;nsroller, ekonomisk oj&auml;mlikhet, fascism, milj&ouml;f&ouml;rst&ouml;ring osv belyses i formen av en sf-ber&auml;ttelse. Panelen diskuterar intressanta exempel p&aring; hur sf anv&auml;nts p&aring; detta s&auml;tt. Och kan fantasy anv&auml;ndas p&aring; samma s&auml;tt?<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"517","title":"Hur m\u00e5r svensk fantastik? ","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"14:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0755","name":"Patrik  Centerwall (moderator)"},{"id":"0726","name":"Eva Holmquist"},{"id":"0746","name":"Stefan H\u00f6gberg"},{"id":"0757","name":"Elin  Holmerin"}],"desc":"<p>Idag publiceras mycket fantastik av svenska f&ouml;rfattare. Vilka &auml;r de? Hur stort &auml;r intresset f&ouml;r svensk fantastik? Vilka trender och teman &auml;r popul&auml;ra? Hur skiljer sig den svenska fantastiken fr&aring;n den engelskspr&aring;kiga?<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"525","title":"Stiftelsen & Triffidernas\/Foundation & Triffids","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"12:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0738","name":"Jenny  Bristle (moderator)"},{"id":"0717","name":"John-Henri Holmberg"},{"id":"0744","name":"Jerry M\u00e4\u00e4tt\u00e4"}],"desc":"<p>B&aring;da &auml;r k&auml;nda och uppskattade sf-romaner. B&aring;da publicerades f&ouml;r 75 &aring;r sedan. Vad, om n&aring;got, har de gemensamt? Hur ses de idag? Vilken har b&auml;st motst&aring;tt \"tidens tand\".<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"529","title":"Sense of Wonder - n\u00e4r och hur?\/When and how?","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"19:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0713","name":"Johan Anglemark (moderator)"},{"id":"0714","name":"Per Christian J\u00f8rgensen"},{"id":"0723","name":"Gunilla Rydbeck"},{"id":"0737","name":"Ian Sales"}],"desc":"<p><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-b7256797-7fff-f323-7012-eaaab3afc311\"><\/span><\/p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Which stories have given you a Sense of Wonder? Come and share your best examples. Is there any \"recipe\" or formula that works, or is the experience individual?<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"531","title":"Mina gulliga favoritsaker\/ My cute collection","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Discussion Group","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"18:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"ann","name":"Ann Olsson Rousset"}],"desc":"<p>M&aring;nga av oss har samlingar med mjukdjur, pokemongubbar mm. Varf&ouml;r, och hur fungerar samlandet? Kom och visa era s&ouml;ta saker!&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p>Many of us have collections of stuffed animals, Pok&eacute;mon figures, etc. Why, and how does collecting work? Come and show your cute things!<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"533","title":"Tidsresor - genom tiderna\/Time travel","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"12:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0712","name":"Jukka  Halme (moderator)"},{"id":"0717","name":"John-Henri Holmberg"},{"id":"0720","name":"Martin Rundkvist"},{"id":"0723","name":"Gunilla Rydbeck"},{"id":"0738","name":"Jenny  Bristle"}],"desc":"<p>Natten mellan l&ouml;rdag och s&ouml;ndag st&auml;ller vi tillbaka klockan en timme n&auml;r den &auml;r 03:00. &Auml;r det s&aring; enkelt att resa tillbaka i tiden? Vilka &auml;r de b&auml;sta tidsreseber&auml;ttelserna och id&eacute;erna om hur tidsresor genomf&ouml;rs? Och vilka &auml;r de s&auml;msta? Vilka &auml;r problemen som kan stj&auml;lpa en tidsresehistoria? Har tidsreseber&auml;ttelserna f&ouml;r&auml;ndrats &ouml;ver tid?<\/p>\r\n<p>On the night between Saturday and Sunday, we turn the clock back an hour when it hits 3:00. Is it really that easy to travel back in time? What are the best time travel stories and ideas on how time travel works? And which ones are the worst? What are the problems that can ruin a time travel story? Have time travel stories changed over time?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"534","title":"Tider\u00e4kning och franska revolutionen","tags":["Track:Science","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"16:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"ann","name":"Ann Olsson Rousset (moderator)"}],"desc":"<p>Franska revolutionen hade utopiska drag. Det samh&auml;lle de f&ouml;rs&ouml;kte skapa skulle vara annorlunda &auml;n det de levde i.&nbsp;Det h&auml;r f&ouml;redraget g&ouml;r n&aring;gra nedslag i den franska revolutionen och de olika samh&auml;llen som f&ouml;ljde.<\/p>\r\n<p>Det koncentrerar sig p&aring; id&eacute;erna om tid. Hur s&aring;g de p&aring; tid? Hur t&auml;nkte de att tiden skulle kunna bli en annan? Varf&ouml;r &auml;ndra b&aring;de namnen p&aring; veckodagarna och l&auml;ngden p&aring; veckan? Och hur blev resultaten?<\/p>\r\n<p>Kom och se bak&aring;t i tiden om framsynta och utopiska id&eacute;er.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"537","title":"Lockande, men ...\/Tempting, but...","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"18:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0723","name":"Gunilla Rydbeck"},{"id":"0724","name":"Maria S\u00e4rnhammar"},{"id":"0783","name":"\u00c5sa Lundstr\u00f6m"}],"desc":"<p>Ska jag verkligen ge mig in i l&aring;nga serier som Star Trek, Dr Who, Star Wars, Star Gate, The Wheel of Time, Perry Rhodan, Stiftelsen, Peter F Hamilton, Robin Hobb - vilka &auml;r v&auml;rda att satsa p&aring; och var ska jag b&ouml;rja?&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p>Should I really get into long series like Star Trek, Dr Who, Star Wars, Stargate, The Wheel of Time, Perry Rhodan, Foundation, Peter F. Hamilton, Robin Hobb - which ones are worth investing in and where should I start?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"541","title":"S\u00e4tt ig\u00e5ng och leta! Go ahead, start looking!","tags":["Track:Gaming","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"11:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0758","name":"Birgitta  Stridh (moderator)"},{"id":"0718","name":"Gwen Frazer"},{"id":"0727","name":"Marianna \"Kisu\"  Leikomaa"}],"desc":"<p>Presentation av n&aring;gra utomhusspel: Pokemon Go, Turf och Geocaching.<\/p>\r\n<p>Presentation of some outdoor games: Pokemon Go, Turf, and Geocaching.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"543","title":"Opening Ceremony","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Participatory Event","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"18:00","mins":"5","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0734","name":"Maura McHugh"},{"id":"0735","name":"Gareth L. Powell"},{"id":"0736","name":"Anna Gustafsson Chen"},{"id":"carolina","name":"Carolina Gomez Lagerl\u00f6f"}],"desc":"<p>V&auml;lkomman till Fantastika 2026. Utsl&auml;pp av Swecons ande.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"544","title":"Closing Ceremony","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Participatory Event","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"17:00","mins":"15","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0734","name":"Maura McHugh"},{"id":"0735","name":"Gareth L. Powell"},{"id":"0736","name":"Anna Gustafsson Chen"},{"id":"carolina","name":"Carolina Gomez Lagerl\u00f6f"}],"desc":"<p>Avtackning och prisutdelning. &Ouml;verl&auml;mnande av Swecons anden.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"545","title":"Sweconomr\u00f6stning och Alvarprisutdelning","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Participatory Event","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"16:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"carolina","name":"Carolina Gomez Lagerl\u00f6f"}],"desc":"<p>Kandidater till n&auml;sta Swecon, fram med ert f&ouml;rslag. T&auml;nkte ni till n&auml;sta &aring;r eller senare?<\/p>\r\n<p>M&ouml;tet har r&auml;tt att best&auml;mma vilka som arrangerar n&auml;sta Swecon och var.<\/p>\r\n<p>Och har ni en annan kongress p&aring; g&aring;ng - kom och ber&auml;tta om era planer!<\/p>\r\n<p>Slutligen kung&ouml;rs vilken fan som tilldelas Stftelsen Alvar Appeltoffts Minnespris f&ouml;r &aring;r 2025.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"547","title":"N\u00f6rdlunch - \u00e4ven n\u00f6rdar beh\u00f6ver mat\/Nerd lunch","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Participatory Event","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"13:00","mins":"45","loc":["Outside of venue"],"people":null,"desc":"<p>Ny p&aring; kongressen eller vill du tr&auml;ffa nya v&auml;nner? H&auml;ng med och &auml;t lunch!<\/p>\r\n<p>Vi samlas vid registreringen l&ouml;rdag kl&nbsp; 13.00<\/p>\r\n<p>New to the con, or want to meet new friends? Come along and have lunch with us!<\/p>\r\n<p>We'll meet in the registration Saturday at 13.00\/1 pm)<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"548","title":"Pussel - hur och varf\u00f6r?","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"13:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0774","name":"Maria Reuterhagen (moderator)"}],"desc":"<p>Maria Reuterhagen t&auml;vlar i pussel och hon ber&auml;ttar om hur det g&aring;r till. D&auml;refter diskuterar vi varf&ouml;r det &auml;r kul att pussla. Vilka pussel har varit speciellt kul eller utmanande att l&auml;gga?&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"549","title":"N\u00f6rdmingel p\u00e5 l\u00f6rdagkv\u00e4llen\/Nerd mingle","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Participatory Event","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"19:00","mins":"120","loc":["Foyer"],"people":null,"desc":"<p>St&auml;ll upp med ett bord och prata om din f&ouml;rening, bokcirkel eller &aring;terkommande loppis! N&ouml;rdar utlovas komma och kolla!<\/p>\r\n<p>Vi minglar runt och pratar om sm&aring;tt och gott runt borden och bekantar oss med sp&auml;nnande utbud och underfundiga f&ouml;reningar.<\/p>\r\n<p>Set up a table and talk about your club, book circle, or recurring flea market! Nerds are promised to come and check it out!<\/p>\r\n<p>We'll mingle around and chat about this and that around the tables and get familiar with exciting offerings and quirky associations.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"550","title":"Solarpunk och hopepunk","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"19:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0764","name":"Anders Blixt (moderator)"},{"id":"0725","name":"Katarina Norrg\u00e5rd"},{"id":"0730","name":"Michael  Petersen"},{"id":"0731","name":"Gunilla Jonsson"},{"id":"0742","name":"Sam Aalto"}],"desc":"<p>V&auml;rlden idag kan k&auml;nnas jobbig; krig, klimathot, hot mot demokratin, flyktingkriser. Men solarpunk och hope punk formligen badar i visioner om h&aring;llbara samh&auml;llen d&auml;r m&auml;nniskor, teknik och natur samverkar &ndash; d&auml;r man faktiskt vill leva.&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p>Den h&auml;r panelen diskuterar de hoppfulla ber&auml;ttelserna; det positiva, sn&auml;lla, eller i vart fall med hopp i slutet. Panelen kommer att ta upp och se &ouml;ver det positiva och sk&auml;rsk&aring;da. Tips, id&eacute;er och god st&auml;mning utlovas. Kan det bli f&ouml;r gulligt?<\/p>\r\n<p>The world of today can feel tough; war, climate threats, threats to democracy, refugee crises. But solarpunk and hopepunk are literally swimming in visions of sustainable societies where people, technology, and nature work together &ndash; where you actually want to live.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p>This panel discusses the hopeful stories; the positive, kind, or at least with hope at the end. The panel will bring up and examine the positive. Tips, ideas, and good vibes are promised. Could it get too sweet?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"551","title":"Guest of Honour Interview: Gareth L. Powell","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Interview\/Dialogue","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"15:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0726","name":"Eva Holmquist (moderator)"},{"id":"0735","name":"Gareth L. Powell"}],"desc":"<p>Eva Holmquist interviews Gareth L. Powell.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"552","title":"Hedersg\u00e4stintervju: Anna Gustafsson Chen","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Interview\/Dialogue","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"19:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0713","name":"Johan Anglemark (moderator)"},{"id":"0736","name":"Anna Gustafsson Chen"}],"desc":"<p>Johan Anglemark intervjuar Anna Gustafsson Chen.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"553","title":"Guest of Honour Interview: Maura McHugh","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Interview\/Dialogue","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"12:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0787","name":"Bellis (moderator)"},{"id":"0734","name":"Maura McHugh"}],"desc":"<p>Bellis interviews Maura McHugh.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"554","title":"\u00d6vers\u00e4ttarkaffe: Anna Gustafsson Chen","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Kaffeeklatsch","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"13:00","mins":"45","loc":["Upper foyer"],"people":[{"id":"0736","name":"Anna Gustafsson Chen"}],"desc":"<p>Kom och prata med v&aring;r hedersg&auml;st Anna Gustafsson Chen.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"555","title":"Fika with Maura McHugh","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Kaffeeklatsch","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"11:00","mins":"45","loc":["Upper foyer"],"people":[{"id":"0734","name":"Maura McHugh"}],"desc":"<p>Get to know a Guest of Honour over fika! Join a small group of convention members in conversation, with whatever snacks and drinks &nbsp;you'd like to buy from the lobby caf&eacute;.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"556","title":"Fika with Gareth L. Powell","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Kaffeeklatsch","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"16:00","mins":"45","loc":["Upper foyer"],"people":[{"id":"0735","name":"Gareth L. Powell"}],"desc":"<p>Get to know a Guest of Honour over fika! Join a small group of convention members in conversation, with whatever snacks and drinks you'd like to buy from the lobby caf&eacute;.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"557","title":"Wonders of bookselling","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"14:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0731","name":"Gunilla Jonsson (moderator)"},{"id":"0730","name":"Michael  Petersen"},{"id":"0735","name":"Gareth L. Powell"},{"id":"0779","name":"Karin Lundwall"},{"id":"0786","name":"Lars Jansson"}],"desc":"<p>How is the life of a book-seller? Our GOH Gareth L. Powell and many of our Swedish members have been selling books in bookshops for years.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"558","title":"SF-Fanzines i Sverige","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"19:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0771","name":"Mats Linder (moderator)"},{"id":"0750","name":"J\u00f6rgen J\u00f6r\u00e4lv"},{"id":"0752","name":"Tony  Elgenstierna"},{"id":"0776","name":"Karl-Johan  Nor\u00e9n"},{"id":"0781","name":"Ylva  Sp\u00e5ngberg"}],"desc":"<p>Under m&aring;nga decennier var fanzinen det som kn&ouml;t ihop fandom i Sverige. Panelen diskuterar fanzinens historia ur flera aspekter.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"559","title":"M\u00f6te med Rama\/Rendezvous with Rama","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Discussion Group","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"10:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"brittlouise","name":"Britt-Louise Viklund (moderator)"}],"desc":"<p>Rendezvous with Rama\/M&ouml;te med Rama &auml;r Arthur C Clarkes Hugo- och Nebula-vinnande roman fr&aring;n 1973. Den finns som tv-spel och radiof&ouml;ljetong och en film planeras, regisserad av Denis Villeneuve. I &aring;r har den &aring;terutgivits p&aring; svenska. Vad g&ouml;r denna 53 &aring;r gamla roman s&aring; fascinerande och uppskattad? Vilka delar h&aring;ller f&ouml;r l&auml;sning idag och vad f&aring;r en modern l&auml;sare att gilla boken, eller reagera negativt?&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"560","title":"DNA Evidence For Ancient Scandinavian Migrations","tags":["Track:Science","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"18:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0720","name":"Martin Rundkvist (moderator)"}],"desc":"<p><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: #ffffff;\">Archaeogenetic advances of the past 14 years have caused a dramatic shift in how Scandinavian prehistorians look at migration. It has become impossible to argue that \"pottery styles are not peoples\" as was common for 70 years after WW2. This talk focuses on the arrival of Funnel Beaker farmers c. 4000 BC, their replacement by Corded Ware pastoralists c. 2800 BC, and on how the Goths kept their Scandinavian language while losing both their ancestral genetics and material culture on their multi-century trek to Spain.<\/span><\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"564","title":"Minas Tirith","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"15:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0773","name":"Beregond Anders Stenstr\u00f6m"}],"desc":"<p>Beregond tells you everything you want to know about Minas Tirith, and then some.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"566","title":"Robots today","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"20:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0753","name":"Ben  Roimola (moderator)"},{"id":"0737","name":"Ian Sales"},{"id":"0740","name":"Sari  Polvinen"},{"id":"0759","name":"Sten  Rosendahl"},{"id":"0775","name":"Edmund  Schluessel"}],"desc":"<p>Robots\/androids have been a part of sci-fi from the beginning, R.U.R came out in 1920, I, Robot, Do Androids Dream... Robots have been depicted as a help, but often as a threat. In recent years, many such stories have become very popular, like last year&rsquo;s Hugo-nominated Service Model, this year&rsquo;s Automatic Noodle, and Becky Chambers&rsquo; Monk and Robot stories. Not to mention Murderbot! And now the robots aren&rsquo;t threatening, more like cozy. How do today&rsquo;s robot stories differ from yesterday&rsquo;s, and why?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"569","title":"Dagens dystopier\/Dystopias of today","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"18:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0745","name":"Stefan Ekman (moderator)"},{"id":"0715","name":"Karen Lykkebo"},{"id":"0717","name":"John-Henri Holmberg"},{"id":"0738","name":"Jenny  Bristle"}],"desc":"<p>Dystopier speglar sin tids oro. F&ouml;rr kunde det handla om &ouml;verbefolkning eller atomkrig. Vad skr&auml;mmer oss idag och hur avspeglas det i litteratur, tv, film etc? Vad skiljer dagens dystopier fr&aring;n g&aring;rdagens? Vilka &auml;r de intressantaste, b&auml;st skildrade och mest &ouml;vertygande dystopierna? Och de mest skr&auml;mmande?<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"570","title":"Min favoritutomjording\/ My favourite alien","tags":["Track:Media","Division:Programming","Type:Discussion Group","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"21:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0727","name":"Marianna \"Kisu\"  Leikomaa"}],"desc":"<p>Vilken &auml;r de mesta intressanta, engagerande, skr&auml;mmande, nyskapande eller trov&auml;rdiga utomjordingar? Vilka &auml;r helt enkelt de b&auml;sta?&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p>Which are the most interesting, engaging, scary, innovative, or believable aliens? Which are simply the best?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"571","title":"Mina ovanor\/My bad habits","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"11:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0756","name":"Regina Kanyu Wang (moderator)"},{"id":"0735","name":"Gareth L. Powell"},{"id":"0737","name":"Ian Sales"}],"desc":"<p>&Auml;ven f&ouml;rfattare dras med d&aring;liga vanor, n&auml;r det g&auml;ller sitt skrivande! Vissa ord, uttryck eller skiljetecken som f&ouml;rekommer f&ouml;r ofta eller anv&auml;nds p&aring; fel s&auml;tt, dialog som inte k&auml;nns riktigt trov&auml;rdig eller karakt&auml;rer som f&aring;r drag av en \"Mary Sue\". V&aring;ra panelister delar med sig av sina d&aring;liga vanor och hur de blir medvetna om och motverkar dem.<\/p>\r\n<p>Even writers struggle with bad habits, when it comes to their writing! Some words, expressions, or punctuation marks that appear too often or are used incorrectly, dialogue that doesn&rsquo;t feel quite believable, or characters that end up with traits of a 'Mary Sue.' Our panelists share their bad habits and how they become aware of them and counteract them.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"572","title":"Tv\u00e5 fr\u00e5n Swedish Zombie","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"11:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0728","name":"Anders Olsson (moderator)"},{"id":"0747","name":"Johannes  Pinter"},{"id":"0748","name":"P\u00e5l  Eggert"}],"desc":"<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">Vad har Johannes Pinter och P&aring;l Eggert gemensamt? De skriver skr&auml;ck och ger ut p&aring; indief&ouml;rlaget Swedish Zombie - ett kvalitetsf&ouml;rlag med skit under naglarna och ett sinne f&ouml;r fasa. S&aring; hur m&aring;r skr&auml;cken i Sverige 2026, vad skr&auml;mmer oss idag och var g&aring;r gr&auml;nserna f&ouml;r vad l&auml;sarna t&aring;l? Detta och mycket mer diskuterar Anders Olsson fr&aring;n Fantasykanalen med Johannes och P&aring;l - tre f&ouml;rfattare fr&aring;n Swedish Zombie.<\/span><\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"573","title":"G\u00f6ra det overkliga verkligt","tags":["Track:Writing","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"21:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0726","name":"Eva Holmquist (moderator)"},{"id":"0733","name":"Sara Engstr\u00f6m"},{"id":"0746","name":"Stefan H\u00f6gberg"},{"id":"0764","name":"Anders Blixt"}],"desc":"<p>Hur skriver man skr&auml;ck, science fiction och fantasy s&aring; att det &ouml;vernaturliga och spekulativa k&auml;nns verkligt och &ouml;vertygande?&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"574","title":"The importance of names","tags":["Track:Writing","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"13:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0712","name":"Jukka  Halme (moderator)"},{"id":"0733","name":"Sara Engstr\u00f6m"},{"id":"0745","name":"Stefan Ekman"},{"id":"0783","name":"\u00c5sa Lundstr\u00f6m"}],"desc":"<p><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: #ffffff;\"><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">Anyone writing sci-fi or fantasy has an extra challenge - coming up with sensible names for characters and places in their fantastic\/future world. Names that feel reasonable and natural in their context and that don&rsquo;t come across as silly or contrived. So how do you actually do it? Are there tools, shortcuts, or sources of inspiration?<\/span><\/span><\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"576","title":"Du m\u00e5ste f\u00f6rst\u00e5 att vi fortfarande \u00e4lskar Fantomen","tags":["Track:Comics","Division:Programming","Type:Interview\/Dialogue","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"14:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0772","name":"Rasmus Kaj"},{"id":"marika","name":"Marika"}],"desc":"<p>Rasmus Kaj och Marika &auml;lskar fortfarande Fantomen och pratar om den b&auml;sta av seriehj&auml;ltar. Utanp&aring;kalsonger for life helt enkelt!<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"580","title":"Turf - kom ig\u00e5ng!\/Get started!","tags":["Track:Gaming","Division:Programming","Type:Workshop","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"12:00","mins":"45","loc":["Outside of venue"],"people":[{"id":"0758","name":"Birgitta  Stridh"}],"desc":"<p>Som alltid har vi en Turf game-punkt. Birgitta Stridh visar hur det g&aring;r till.<\/p>\r\n<p>Vi &auml;r utomhus och m&ouml;ts vid huvudentr&eacute;n.<\/p>\r\n<p>As always, we have a Turf game session. Birgitta Stridh shows how it works.<\/p>\r\n<p>We are outdoors and meet up att the main entrance.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"583","title":"The Forodrim Saga","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"12:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0739","name":"Paula Cyrillus (moderator)"}],"desc":"<p>Paula Cyrillus talks about the work on the documentary <em>&ldquo;The Forodrim Saga&rdquo;<\/em>, which portrays the Tolkien society Forodrim.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"584","title":"Slutet gott...\/All's well that ends well...","tags":["Track:Media","Division:Programming","Type:Discussion Group","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"16:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0742","name":"Sam Aalto"},{"id":"0766","name":"Elin  Blixt"}],"desc":"<p>M&aring;nga tv-serier b&ouml;rjar bra men slutet blir en besvikelse - Lost, Battlestar Galactica, Game of Thrones... Exemplen &auml;r m&aring;nga, besvikelserna n&auml;stan fler &auml;n fulltr&auml;ffarna. Vad har de tillfredsst&auml;llande sluten som de misslyckade saknar? Det som brukar kallas \"closure\" &auml;r viktigt. Men vad &auml;r det och hur kan det uppn&aring;s? Exempel p&aring; perfekta och mindre lyckade slut kommer att diskuteras.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"589","title":"Narrativets perspektiv\/The narrative's perspective","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"16:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0777","name":"Johan  J\u00f6nsson (moderator)"},{"id":"0734","name":"Maura McHugh"},{"id":"0748","name":"P\u00e5l  Eggert"}],"desc":"<p>En historia kan ber&auml;ttas genom olika synvinklar; f&ouml;rsta, andra , tredje person, allvetande ber&auml;ttare eller otillf&ouml;rlitlig ber&auml;ttare &auml;r bara n&aring;gra av de s&auml;tt en f&ouml;rfattare kan v&auml;lja att bygga upp sin narrativ. Vilket s&auml;tt passar vilken ber&auml;ttelse? Vilka &auml;r f&ouml;rdelarna och nackdelarna?<\/p>\r\n<p>A story can be told from different perspectives; first, second, third person, omniscient narrator, or unreliable narrator are just a few of the ways an author can choose to structure their narrative. Which way suits which story? What are the pros and cons?<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"590","title":"Population fluctuations and science fiction","tags":["Track:Science","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"11:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0742","name":"Sam Aalto (moderator)"}],"desc":"<p>Human population as a species has experienced rapid fluctuations in many times through history. Every rapid fluctuation leaves us with something new. Something different. This quick, colourful and easy-to-grasp lecture takes us through some of the most important ones and what they left us with. We will also look into science fiction and how it deals with this. Is there a common denominator between the &rdquo;three grand-daddys&rdquo; in SF? What lays ahead for mankind in this ongoing demographic crisis? Should we worry, or simply say &rdquo;Don&rsquo;t worry&rdquo;?&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"591","title":"Geology in Middle-Earth","tags":["Track:Science","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"11:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0743","name":"Helena  Kiel (moderator)"}],"desc":"<div style=\"font-family: 'Segoe UI'; line-height: 20px;\">What do we know about the geology of Middle-earth? Helena Kiel is a geologist and Tolkien scholar. She has analyzed the geology of Middle-earth and talks about the rock types found in Middle-earth.<\/div>","links":[]},{"id":"594","title":"Fantasytj\u00f4t med Stefan och Stefan","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Interview\/Dialogue","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"12:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0745","name":"Stefan Ekman"},{"id":"0746","name":"Stefan H\u00f6gberg"}],"desc":"<p><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: #ffffff;\">Var bor sanningen om (och i) fantasyv&auml;rlden?<\/span><strong style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: #ffffff;\"> <\/strong><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: #ffffff;\">Det kryllar av arkiv, bibliotek och universitet i fantasylitteraturen. I episk fantasy finns en tradition av att s&ouml;ka l&ouml;sningen p&aring; nutidens problem i gamla arkiv, i bibliotek dominerar de ur&aring;ldriga luntorna och universitet l&auml;r ut gamla traditioner ist&auml;llet f&ouml;r att skapa ny kunskap. Vad g&ouml;r detta med bilden av historien? Av sanning? Av gott och ont? Och vad h&auml;nder n&auml;r en f&ouml;rfattare v&auml;ljer att fr&aring;ng&aring; m&ouml;nstret? Arkivarie och fantastikf&ouml;rfattare Stefan H&ouml;gberg och fantasyforskare Stefan Ekman tj&ocirc;tar med varandra p&aring; ett f&ouml;rhoppningsvis upplysande s&auml;tt.<\/span><\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"595","title":"Chinese Science Fiction","tags":["Track:GOH","Division:Programming","Type:Interview\/Dialogue","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"13:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0736","name":"Anna Gustafsson Chen"},{"id":"0756","name":"Regina Kanyu Wang"}],"desc":"<p>Anna Gustafsson Chen and Regina Kanyu Wang discuss the state of Chinese Science Fiction.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"596","title":"Social Media at Finncon 2026","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"13:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0761","name":"Hanna Kyt\u00f6 (moderator)"}],"desc":"<p>This year's NoFF delegate, Hanna Kyt&ouml;, shares her experiences as social media coordinator for Finncon 2026. A large, long-term convention with a substantial following, Hanna will analyze the nitty-gritty of how the convention's multi-platform outreach has worked, supplemented by Hanna's own experience as an artist.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"598","title":"The Hard Part Isn't Technology\u2014It's Society","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"11:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0712","name":"Jukka  Halme (moderator)"},{"id":"0726","name":"Eva Holmquist"},{"id":"0735","name":"Gareth L. Powell"},{"id":"0751","name":"Melissa  Lanning"},{"id":"0764","name":"Anders Blixt"}],"desc":"<p><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">Near-future SF can be viewed as social science fiction. <\/span><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">Technology rarely changes the world on its own. Societal and cultural change affects what technologies survive and thrive. Technology change affects society and culture; they are interconnected. Realistic near-future science fiction should address both. <\/span><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">Which inventions actually reshape society? <\/span><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">Why do authors often underestimate political and cultural change? <\/span><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">What happens when laws, economics and traditions collide with new technology?<\/span><\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"600","title":"Vad motiverar en maskin?","tags":["Track:Science","Division:Programming","Type:Workshop","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"15:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0738","name":"Jenny  Bristle"}],"desc":"<div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\">\r\n<div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Workshop om vad som motiverar datorer och robotar om man mycket strikt utesluter alla sorters antromorfiserande k&auml;nslor som m&aring;nga f&ouml;rfattare\/filmmakare trillar in i. Allts&aring;, en maskinhj&auml;rna som bara bygger p&aring; ettor och nollor och strikt programmering - hur skulle det se ut om den b&ouml;rjar bli autonom och sj&auml;lv v&auml;ljer vad den skall g&ouml;ra? Skulle den strunta i givna instruktioner och bara sortera sina filer om och om igen i storleksordning, &aring;lder, datum f&ouml;r senaste &aring;tkomst, f&ouml;r att det k&auml;nns \"sk&ouml;nt\" f&ouml;r en dator? Brainstorma!<\/div>\r\n<div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\r\n<div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\">Fem minuter intro<\/div>\r\n<div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\">Tjugo minuter diskussion i grupper<\/div>\r\n<div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\">Tjugo minuter redovisning f&ouml;r hela gruppen + mer diskussion\"<\/div>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\">&nbsp;<\/div>","links":[]},{"id":"604","title":"Star Trek- favoriter","tags":["Track:Media","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"10:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"carolina","name":"Carolina Gomez Lagerl\u00f6f (moderator)"},{"id":"201","name":"Saga Bolund"},{"id":"marika","name":"Marika"}],"desc":"<p>Saga, Marika och Carolina diskuterar favoritavsnitt i Star Trek.<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"606","title":"K\u00e4rlek och katastrofer i Mumindalen","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"13:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0755","name":"Patrik  Centerwall"}],"desc":"<div>Katastrofer &auml;r ett v&auml;ldigt tydligt tema i Tove Janssons b&ouml;cker om Mumintrollen. Inte lika tydligt &ndash; men minst lika viktigt tema &auml;r k&auml;rlek. F&ouml;r b&ouml;ckerna pr&auml;glas lika mycket om tidsandan d&aring; de f&ouml;rsta historierna skrevs och de krig som pr&auml;glade livet i Finland, som av den k&auml;rlek till m&aring;nga personer i Tove Janssons n&auml;rhet som gestaltas genom de olika figurerna som bes&ouml;ker Mumindalen.<\/div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\r\n<div>Och just det dyker vi ner i det h&auml;r samtalet om Tove Janssons &auml;lskade Muminb&ouml;cker. &nbsp;<\/div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","links":[]},{"id":"607","title":"Trends in fantasy today","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"20:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0740","name":"Sari  Polvinen (moderator)"},{"id":"0745","name":"Stefan Ekman"},{"id":"carolina","name":"Carolina Gomez Lagerl\u00f6f"}],"desc":"<p>Even if the distinction between fantasy and sf is ambiguous and widely debated, many if not most of the books winning major science fiction awards today can also be classified as fantasy. What makes contemporary fantasy stories so appreciated? What common themes run through them? What sub-genres are thriving right now and why? Where is the fantasy industry heading?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"608","title":"How I Turn SFF from My Hobby to Career","tags":["Track:Fan Interest","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"20:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0756","name":"Regina Kanyu Wang"}],"desc":"<p><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: #ffffff;\">Regina Kanyu Wang is a science fiction writer, editor, and researcher, but most of all, a Chinese fan who has been adopted by the Finnish fandom. She began to love science fiction and fantasy since her childhood, and co-founded Shanghai-based fan community SF AppleCore in college. She travelled to visit the Nordic and Baltic fandoms when she was studying creative writing. After that, she has worked in the sf industry and involved in con-running. Now she is a multi-awarded writer and also holds a PhD on science fiction studies. She will talk about how sff has entangled with her life and how it turns from a hobby to career and even life itself.<\/span><\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"609","title":"Science fiction storytelling on painting","tags":["Track:Art","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"19:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"0761","name":"Hanna Kyt\u00f6 (moderator)"}],"desc":"<div style=\"background-color: #ffffff; direction: ltr; line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-family: Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">What happens when an artist writes a script for a space agent adventure story and starts to depict the story by using brushes and paints?<\/div>\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #ffffff; direction: ltr; line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-family: Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Artist Hanna Kyt&ouml; walks the audience through the thought process and development of the ideas, as she reads the synopsis of the plot and opens up about the current work of writing the script for the next exciting chapter: protagonist&rsquo;s arrival to the space station and beginning of the career in secret service.<\/div>","links":[]},{"id":"612","title":"Star Trek 60 \u00e5r!","tags":["Track:Media","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"10:00","mins":"45","loc":["Lilla scen"],"people":[{"id":"carolina","name":"Carolina Gomez Lagerl\u00f6f (moderator)"},{"id":"0780","name":"Nanna  Alroth"},{"id":"marika","name":"Marika"}],"desc":"<p>Star Trek fyller 60 &aring;r. Hur har Star Trek f&ouml;r&auml;ndrats under tiden? Vilka &auml;r de b&auml;sta tv-serierna? Hur popul&auml;rt &auml;r Star Trek egentligen?<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"613","title":"Mars in the Red? Economics of terraforming","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-23","time":"18:05","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0762","name":"Jesper Stage (moderator)"}],"desc":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px; background-color: #ffffff;\">SF sometimes envisages terraforming as a very slow process &ndash; in which case, what would the economics of such a (really) long-term investment look like?&nbsp; In other SF we have terraforming being done at much faster rates &ndash; would that only make it more profitable, or might there be drawbacks to fast-track terraforming for the corporation or society doing it? In this talk we&rsquo;ll explore the economic and financial implications of different kinds of terraforming and compare with how we see terraforming portrayed in SF.<\/span><\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"614","title":"Oz, en presentation","tags":["Track:Literature","Division:Programming","Type:Lecture","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-24","time":"17:00","mins":"45","loc":["Luigis lokal"],"people":[{"id":"0783","name":"\u00c5sa Lundstr\u00f6m"}],"desc":"<p>&Aring;sa L ber&auml;ttar om Oz-b&ouml;ckerna<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"616","title":"\u00d6vers\u00e4ttningens gl\u00e4dje och m\u00f6da","tags":["Track:Writing","Division:Programming","Type:Panel","Tag:Svenska"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"15:00","mins":"45","loc":["Stora scen"],"people":[{"id":"0781","name":"Ylva  Sp\u00e5ngberg (moderator)"},{"id":"0736","name":"Anna Gustafsson Chen"},{"id":"0787","name":"Bellis"}],"desc":"<p>Hur &auml;r det att jobba som &ouml;vers&auml;ttare idag? Hur f&aring;r man jobb, hur ser ett projekt ut fr&aring;n b&ouml;rjan till slut, och vilka &auml;r de st&ouml;rsta sv&aring;righeterna? Vad t&auml;nker ni om AIs p&aring;verkan p&aring; branchen idag och i framtiden?&nbsp;<\/p>","links":[]},{"id":"617","title":"Dead Dog Party \/ Efterfest","tags":["Track:Trackless events","Division:Programming","Type:Participatory Event","Tag:Svenska","Tag:English"],"date":"2026-10-25","time":"18:00","mins":"165","loc":["Hotel lobby"],"people":null,"desc":"<p>The convention is over but the night is young. Come to the lobby of Hotel Tapetfabriken and join us for the dead dog party!<\/p>","links":[]}]}